  "deletedAt": null,
  "details": "There are several pieces of feedback asking for specific features to be implemented to fix skirt clipping. I think we should discuss how to achieve this without requesting for specific things to be done, since we are starting from a clean slate.\nI think what we have so far are:\n- Inside colliders: with DynamicBones, this seems  to be the best way to prevent skirt clipping. Inside colliders for PhysBones would be useful for other things too.\n- Angle restrictions and offsets: this would need to move with the legs. I don't think this will work that well for longer skirts, since the end bones will still split apart enough for the leg collider to pass through. Also, locking the axis doesn't look that great.\nAdditionally:\n- Constraints between siblings: could allow skirt bones to behave more like cloth, although I don't know how expensive this would be. Hopefully it is viable with PhysBones magic. This would also improve grabbing skirt bones.",
